# {{.Title}}

A course for [Nabu](https://github.com/mrmxf/nabu).

```bash
nabu doctor    # silent when this folder is ready; otherwise says what to fix
nabu seed      # load content/ into pb_data (run from this folder)
nabu serve     # http://127.0.0.1:8090
nabu build     # static site in dist/ (guest lessons work with no server)
```

To teach a live lesson from this laptop, run `nabu classroom`. It seeds the
course, signs students in by name only, and prints the address and a QR code for
the room. `content/lesson-schedules.yaml` holds the Session they join. Check the
laptop first with `nabu doctor --mode classroom`.

Content lives in `content/{{.Course}}/`. The full authoring guide is the
[nabu-tutorial](https://github.com/mrmxf/nabu-tutorial) course.
{{- if .Library}}

This course builds its own binary with Nabu as a Go library:

```bash
go get github.com/mrmxf/nabu@latest   # first time: adds Nabu to go.mod
go build -o {{.Binary}} .
./{{.Binary}} seed && ./{{.Binary}} serve
```

The web app is a build output of Nabu, not part of the Go module. Fetch the
release that `go.mod` requires (checked against its `checksums.txt`) into
`nabu-web/`, which `main.go` serves:

```bash
go run . web fetch
```
{{- end}}

## Build and deploy with clog

`.clog.yaml` says how CI builds this course, and `.clog-version` pins the
[clog](https://github.com/mrmxf/clog) it uses.
{{- if eq .CI "github"}} `.github/workflows/course.yaml` runs it on GitHub.
{{- else if eq .CI "gitlab"}} `.gitlab-ci.yml` runs it on GitLab.
{{- end}}

```bash
clog build     # checks, then the static site in _clog_build/public
```

Every push builds and checks; nothing deploys until you fill in `ci.targets`
and `ci.infisical` in `.clog.yaml` and switch on `ci.policy.deploy`
(`clog CI --config-help`).
